      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. I'll start with sampling. One thing that's annoying is that the gaps aren't always in the same category—sometimes it's stationary, sometimes it's small kitchen supplies—but they always happen in these tiny, nagging amounts that just seem to \"vanish\" from the reconciliation. It feels less like a single large error and more like a lot of little, unexplained things happening in the background. \n\nAside from sampling, how should I handle the reconciliation of the physical receipts against the digital entries for these specific small amounts? I want to be able to pinpoint exactly where the leak is occurring without spending weeks on it.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
