    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "The desk audit sounds like the right way to go. I'll have the team start matching the hard copies to the digital records for the last three months. \n\nThe main concern is that even when we find the error, it's often just a tiny mismatch—like a receipt for 14.50€ being logged as 14.00€, or a missing small item that doesn't show up on any report at all. It's these little, repetitive inconsistencies that are driving me crazy. Since these aren't large-scale fraud indicators, but rather these persistent, small-scale \"noise\" issues, are there any specific red flags in the data patterns I should look for that might point to intentional manipulation rather than just sloppy administrative errors?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
